{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Focus}
\pard\keepn \b\fs32\cf1 Focus
\par \pard \plain\fs24 The focus can be controlled by clicking on the Mag/Focus icon \{bmc bm3.bmp\} . 
\par 
\par  This will assign focus control to the centre mouse button.  Alternatively it can be set directly by double clicking on the \b WD =\plain\fs24   display in the status bar \{bmc bm4.bmp\}.
\par 
\par \f6\b\cf2 In some places the focus value is displayed as the Working Distance, these two parameters describe the same thing\plain\f6\fs24\cf2 .
\par 
\par \plain\f6\i\fs24 Optibeam\plain\f6\fs24  uses the working distance value to set the lens currents to achieve the required focusing. If \i Optibeam\plain\f6\fs24  is not active the focus is adjusted by controlling the C3 lens current directly.\fs20 
