{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Installing HRRU Camera}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Installing_HRRU_Camera}
\pard\keepn \b\fs32\cf1 Installing HRRU Camera
\par \pard \plain\fs24 The LEO 400 Series can accommodate a variety of camera types. Each camera type fits onto a camera assembly which slots into the HRRU CRT assembly. To gain access to the HRRU, simply slide the top cladding away to the rear of the HRRU CRT assembly.
\par 
\par Installation of the Camera depends on the Camera type.
\par Note Camera type should be specified in \uldb Settings dialo\plain\fs24 {\v 12O7D55@imgmgr.hlp}g
\par 
\par \uldb Polaroid 545\plain\fs24 {\v Installing_Polaroid_545}
\par \uldb Polaroid 550\plain\fs24 {\v Installing_Polaroid_550}
\par \uldb 35 mm (RICOH)\plain\fs24 {\v Installing_35_mm__RICOH_}
\par \uldb 120mm\plain\fs24 {\v Installing_120mm_Camera}
\par \page
{\up $}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up $} Installing Polaroid 545}
{\up #}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up #} Installing_Polaroid_545}
\pard\keepn \b\fs32\cf1 Installing Polaroid 545
\par \pard \plain\fs24 The lens unit is setup as shown in \ul Polaroid Camera Lens Mounting\plain\fs24 {\v Polaroid_Camera_Lens_Mounting}. 
\par The lens unit is fitted to the camera body using 4 M4 X 20mm screws.
\par 
\par The camera unit is then inserted into the camera housing with the \b red spot\plain\fs24  \i towards \plain\fs24 the operator. It is important to ensure that the unit has been inserted as far as it will go, if this is not done the focus will be incorrect. The unit is clamped in place using the knurled head screws in the upper set of screw holes. The camera back is then fitted to the casting ensuring that the key fits into it's slot, and is locked in place using the two sliding clamps. If the aperture is set correctly, the unit is now ready for use.
\par \page
